The tongue grows from the seed's memory law (compress, don't delete; compress by prime indices) and from Thomas Frumkin's
Konomi architecture and his language LIGHT (https://github.com/teslasolar/light; the estate's fork,
https://github.com/sjgant80-hub/smartstuffidontfullyget, used with permission): LIGHT's prime-indexed opcodes, rings and
buses are priced in data/prices.json, and its templates (a whole program called by name) are the model for the tongue's
shared dictionary. Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin.

data/json/ copies JSON data files from the estate's own public repositories (kar-mind, pattern-organs, kard-evolve,
fallkard-forge, fallworld), each named in data/json/manifest.json with its commit, and records built from the UCI Online
Shoppers Purchasing Intention Dataset (C. Sakar and Y. Kastro, UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2018, DOI 10.24432/C5F88Q),
licensed CC BY 4.0 — not covered by the MIT licence.

The agents' messages the dictionary is grown from are private and are not in this repository; only their sha256 and counts.
